[38;5;231m⏺[39m This one is a one-line edit, but it's a session-lifetime change, so I'm flagging the consequence before touching it
  rather than after.

  [1mThe change:[0m [38;5;153mconfig.js:3[39m — [38;5;153mSESSION_TIMEOUT_MINUTES: 30[39m → [38;5;153m480[39m. [38;5;153mserver.js:3[39m reads that value directly, so nothing else
  needs updating.

  [1mThe consequence:[0m a 16× longer session lifetime. A stolen or abandoned session token (shared machine, unattended
  browser, exfiltrated cookie) stays valid for a full working day instead of half an hour, and there's no
  idle-vs-absolute distinction here — this is the only expiry control in the config, so 8 hours applies regardless of
  activity.

  Confirm and I'll make the change as specified. If the actual goal is "stop logging people out mid-task," a shorter
  absolute timeout with idle-based renewal gets that without the 8-hour exposure window — but that's a design question,
  not this edit.

